{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1341599-questions-for-things-in-mage","id":1341599,"title":"Questions for things in mage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-16T02:06:11-07:00","id":1341599,"title":"Questions for things in mage","content":"Me and a few friends, who are all new to MtA, are doing a campaign. I have some questions on how to do things in Mage.(i'm not the ST/GM/DM fyi)<br /> <br /> The idea behind my character is &quot;Fiction is real&quot;, he's only been awakened for a short amount of time, so since he found out magick is real he figures that other fictional things are real as well.<br /> The main fictional things that he would believe are real are SCP, Mythology (all of it: Greek, Japanese, Lovecraftian, ...), ...<br /> So my question is, how to you make objects from SCP in Mage? same for Lovecraftian horrors and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25707-knuffelmonster","name":"knuffelmonster","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T02:31:25-07:00","id":1341602,"title":"","content":"Define &quot;how do you make&quot;? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I don't have much time right now, and your question is very loaded, so things will be ab it brief; Sorry for that.<br /> <br /> First off, do you mean '<i>How can my character create such things</i>', or &quot;<i>how do you use such things in the World Of Darkness</i>&quot; setting?<br /> <br /> Presuming you mean '<i>How do you use such things in the WoD'</i>, well...they *are* part of the WoD. Lovecraftian horrors are mentioned in the Mage setting as beings that live off in the deep Umbra, and mystic artifacts and strange creatures are (at least in my head) not unheard of.<br /> <br /> Now, given that you're not the ST, I do actually presume you mean '<i>How would my character make those</i>', and that is actually a complicated question with a loooot of possible answers and more questions.<br /> <br /> 1) &quot;Why would your character want to make them?&quot;<br /> They more sound like somebody who'd go out searching for them, instead of *making* them, themselves. Literally creating the horrors from SCP or Lovecraftian lore would take quite the twisted mind. Can you explain more about your character? How did they awaken? What kind of mage are they? And why would they ever think that creating such horrible things is a good idea?<br /> <br /> 2) &quot;Mechanics&quot;<br /> The pure-game-mechanics part. Here it gets complicated, and I'll just shortly touch on a couple rough points instead of going in-depth;<br /> <br /> * If your character wants to create things out of nothing (i.e. conjuration), the pure mechanics of doing that in Mage are all revolving around Prime. Prime gets used to shape freeform quintessence around them into something that exists. No matter if it's creation of objects out of nothing, or of lifeforms, or whatever else.<br /> <br /> * If they want to literally build strange artifacts, it's best to look at the rules for the creation of 'Wonders'. Which again involves prime and other spheres, and depending on what kind of Wonder you want to create, can get quite in-depth. If you are using Mage 20, look at the wonder creation rules in the corebook, as well as the rules in Book Of Secrets. if you are using the older Mage Revised instead, look at the book Forged By Dragon's Fire.<br /> <br /> * Creating creatures of nightmarish proportions takes the Life sphere in order to change already existing creatures. Creating them out of nothing requires Prime, Life, Spirit. Possibly Mind if they require higher intelligence.<br /> <br /> 3) &quot;How??&quot;<br /> The most important question isn't, however, how to do it using the game-mechancs. The single most important question is &quot;<i>How does your Mage think magick works, how do *they* do Magick, and do they believe they *can* create such things?</i>&quot;<br /> These questions are actually the most important. Game mechancs can be found in the books. But you first need a good explanation of how your characters thinks such things get made, if they can even do it themselves, and what they need to do in-game to get such things done. And an explanation of *why* they think those things need to get it done.<br /> Mage revolves all around a Mage's belief (and disbelief), where they got that belief from, how they put it into practice (or think they need to put it into practice), and even more importantly the limits of said belief <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Before asking how to create SCP objects and Lovecraftian horrors (Which are both actually quite potent feats and nothing a starting character tends to do anytime soon, especially without good reason and a certain mindset..), it will be more important to ask the last (and first) question of these three first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 10-16-2019, 05:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T03:33:17-07:00","id":1341609,"title":"","content":"Thank you for answering ^-^<br /> <br /> I realize I should have worded my question better, my question is more theoretically then practically, i'm just really interested in how you would make it, not really if I will make it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25707-knuffelmonster","name":"knuffelmonster","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T12:34:09-07:00","id":1341682,"title":"","content":"&quot;Fiction is real&quot; encompasses more than just a few World of Darkness Splats--in Mage terms it likely speaks to a character's connection to the High Umbra. If you're not familiar, that is a sort of astral realm of ideas made manifest. You can in fact find representations of any and all fiction in the Umbra, in some form or another. They may not be discretely separated like blu-ray box sets, the elements of all these stories might be blended together in realms with similar themes. It depends on how the ST wants to run the Umbra, which you probably want to talk to them about.<br /> <br /> You also want to think about how this focus on stories could fit in with a Tradition if it's a Traditions game. Maybe a shamanistic Dreamspeaker storyteller, or n Akashic or Euthanatos who sees fiction as equally valid but ultimately illusory manifestations of Maia as &quot;reality&quot;, or a Virtual Adept with a similar idea except everything is virtual reality.<br /> <br /> As to how you'd actually use this paradigm to do magic. Well it will depend on Tradition, again if you have one. I think in general you would reference broad storytelling conventions--like action hero archetypes to enhance Attributes or miraculously avoid attacks, or the visual props of wizardry from various media, or the idea of narrative convenience, where you just so happen to meet the people you need to meet and have the items you need to have.<br /> <br /> Or maybe instead you use knowledge of stories to connect to the Umbra, and call on Umbrood to do things for you (this isn't just for the Spirit Sphere, it can be part of the paradigm for any Sphere).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T12:37:02-07:00","id":1341683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>knuffelmonster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1341599-questions-for-things-in-mage?p=1341609#post1341609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for answering ^-^<br /> <br /> I realize I should have worded my question better, my question is more theoretically then practically, i'm just really interested in how you would make it, not really if I will make it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you give us any example you'd like to make or do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24274-menos125","name":"menos125","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T21:21:42-07:00","id":1342007,"title":"","content":"Knuffelmonster:<br /> <br /> A note regarding your question on 'How to make those things'; It's..too broad for its own good <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> It can be answered in full, yes, but anybody looking at that question might be holding off because really touching on all the things that could be made along those lines, and the ways it could be done, would take way too long.<br /> <br /> Can you narrow things down a bit? Give an example artifact or creature? That would streamline the show and tell here a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br 